# rc.conf.local — OpenBSD daemon configuration (rc.conf(8)).
#
# Copyright (c) 2026 The wtfbsd contributors. BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE).
#
# rc.conf(8): /etc/rc.conf.local holds variable=value assignments that
# override /etc/rc.conf; the file is read by rc(8) on every boot and every
# time an rc.d(8) script is run. A daemon is enabled by setting its
# <daemon>_flags variable to an empty value (it then runs with the default
# arguments); "<daemon>_flags=NO" disables it.
#
# OpenBSD has no rc.conf.d: there is one rc.conf.local per root. The
# profile overlay ships a FRAGMENT that build.sh appends to this file, so
# the base settings live here and the profile settings in the fragment.
#
# The name of the host is NOT here: on OpenBSD it is /etc/myname (the
# placeholder is substituted by build.sh).

# Package daemons started at boot, in the order given (rc.conf(8),
# pkg_scripts). The profile fragment adds the daemons it needs.
pkg_scripts=""
